          "id": "el-1790478899888",
          "type": "collectible",
          "content": "<b>Algebra</b> is math where letters stand for numbers.\nIt lets you:\n<b>Write a rule</b> → Pay = 15h works for any number of hours.\n<b>Find an unknown</b> → 82,500y = 412,500, so y = 5.\n<b>Algebra turns data into knowledge.</b>\n## SOURCES\nhttps://www.jchs.harvard.edu/sites/default/files/interactive-item/files/Harvard_JCHS_State_of_the_Nations_Housing_2025_Press_Release.pdf\nhttps://www.cnbc.com/2022/06/13/service-workers-report-unpredictable-schedules-and-it-impacts-more-than-pay.html\nhttps://www.propublica.org/article/the-secret-irs-files-trove-of-never-before-seen-records-reveal-how-the-wealthiest-avoid-income-tax\nhttps://www.oxfam.org/en/press-releases/billionaires-emit-more-carbon-pollution-90-minutes-average-person-does-lifetime\nhttps://americansfortaxfairness.org/billionaire-clans-spend-nearly-2-billion-2024-elections/\n<b>Example (not data):</b> $15/hour wage, 75-year lifetime, $50 donation, $8,250/year savings (10% of $82,500).",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 50,
          "width": 82,
          "height": 60,
          "rotation": 0,
          "scale": 1,
